<main id="main">
<h1>Backtesting — Historical Strategy Simulation</h1>

<div class="hero">
  <p class="subtitle">A modular backtesting engine for historical strategy evaluation</p>
  <p>This sub-module provides a complete event-driven loop that replays trading strategies
    against historical market data. It manages portfolio state, executes trades, computes
    risk-adjusted performance metrics, and benchmarks results against SPY.</p>
</div>

<div class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">10</div><div class="label">Files</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">1,115</div><div class="label">Lines</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">5</div><div class="label">Performance Metrics</div></div>
  <div class="stat-box"><div class="num">Python</div><div class="label">Language</div></div>
</div>

<p>
  <span class="badge blue">🔵 Event-Driven</span>
  <span class="badge green">🟢 Long/Short</span>
  <span class="badge yellow">🟡 Multi-Ticker</span>
  <span class="badge red">🔴 Risk Metrics</span>
</p>

<div class="intro-box">
  <h3>🔋 What &amp; Why</h3>
  <p>The backtesting engine is like a <strong>flight simulator for trading strategies</strong>.
    Just as pilots practice manoeuvres in a simulator before flying a real aircraft, this module
    lets you replay your AI-driven trading strategy against real historical data — without risking
    actual capital. It faithfully models cash flow, margin requirements, and short-selling
    mechanics so the performance numbers you see are as close to reality as possible.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Analogy deep-dive…</summary>
    <p>Imagine you could rewind the stock market to any date, hand your strategy a portfolio of
      cash, and press "play." Each trading day the strategy receives market data, makes
      buy/sell/short/cover decisions, and the engine settles every trade exactly as a brokerage
      would. At the end it hands you a scorecard — Sharpe ratio, max drawdown, exposure
      breakdown — so you know whether your strategy would have survived real-world turbulence.</p>
  </details>
</div>

<nav class="toc" id="toc"></nav>

<!-- ───────────── Architecture ───────────── -->
<h2 id="architecture">Architecture</h2>
<div class="diagram-container">
<pre class="mermaid">
classDiagram
    class BacktestEngine {
        +tickers: list
        +portfolio: Portfolio
        +controller: AgentController
        +executor: TradeExecutor
        +__init__()
        +_prefetch_data()
        +run_backtest()
        +get_portfolio_values()
    }
    class Portfolio {
        +cash: float
        +positions: dict
        +margin_requirement: float
        +apply_long_buy()
        +apply_long_sell()
        +apply_short_open()
        +apply_short_cover()
        +get_snapshot()
        +get_realized_gains()
    }
    class AgentController {
        +invoke_agent()
        +normalize_output()
        +validate_actions()
    }
    class TradeExecutor {
        +execute_buy()
        +execute_sell()
        +execute_short()
        +execute_cover()
    }
    class PerformanceMetricsCalculator {
        +sharpe_ratio()
        +sortino_ratio()
        +max_drawdown()
    }
    class OutputBuilder {
        +format_daily_row()
        +build_summary_table()
    }
    class BenchmarkCalculator {
        +compute_spy_return()
    }
    BacktestEngine --> Portfolio : owns
    BacktestEngine --> AgentController : delegates decisions
    BacktestEngine --> TradeExecutor : delegates trades
    BacktestEngine --> PerformanceMetricsCalculator : computes metrics
    BacktestEngine --> OutputBuilder : formats output
    BacktestEngine --> BenchmarkCalculator : compares vs SPY
    TradeExecutor --> Portfolio : mutates
    PerformanceMetricsCalculator ..> Portfolio : reads equity curve
</pre>
</div>

<!-- ───────────── Key Classes ───────────── -->
<h2 id="key-classes">Key Classes &amp; Functions</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Component</th><th>File</th><th>LOC</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>BacktestEngine</code></td><td>engine.py</td><td>194</td><td>Orchestrates the full backtest loop: date iteration, agent calls, trade execution, value tracking</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>Portfolio</code></td><td>portfolio.py</td><td>195</td><td>Manages cash, long/short positions, margin, cost basis, realized gains</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>Action</code> enum</td><td>types.py</td><td>105</td><td>Defines <code>buy | sell | short | cover | hold</code> action variants</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>AgentController</code></td><td>controller.py</td><td>67</td><td>Invokes the trading agent, normalizes raw outputs, validates action legality</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>TradeExecutor</code></td><td>trader.py</td><td>39</td><td>Translates agent decisions into portfolio mutations (buy/sell/short/cover)</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>PerformanceMetricsCalculator</code></td><td>metrics.py</td><td>77</td><td>Computes Sharpe, Sortino, max drawdown from the equity curve</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>calculate_portfolio_value</code></td><td>valuation.py</td><td>82</td><td>Marks positions to market; computes long/short/gross/net exposure</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>compute_exposures</code></td><td>valuation.py</td><td>—</td><td>Returns exposure breakdown as a dict for risk monitoring</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>OutputBuilder</code></td><td>output.py</td><td>98</td><td>Formats daily results and final summary as rich terminal tables</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>BenchmarkCalculator</code></td><td>benchmarks.py</td><td>32</td><td>Computes SPY buy-and-hold return over the same date range</td></tr>
  <tr><td>CLI entry point</td><td>cli.py</td><td>172</td><td>Argparse CLI: analyst selection, model provider, date range, tickers</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>PerformanceMetrics</code></td><td>types.py</td><td>—</td><td>TypedDict holding Sharpe, Sortino, max drawdown, long/short ratio, exposure</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ───────────── Data Flow ───────────── -->
<h2 id="data-flow">Data Flow</h2>
<div class="diagram-container">
<pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI as cli.py
    participant Engine as BacktestEngine
    participant AC as AgentController
    participant Agent as Trading Agent
    participant TE as TradeExecutor
    participant P as Portfolio
    participant V as Valuation
    participant M as Metrics
    participant O as OutputBuilder

    CLI->>Engine: run_backtest(tickers, dates, config)
    Engine->>Engine: _prefetch_data(tickers + SPY)
    loop Each business day
        Engine->>AC: get_decisions(date, prices, portfolio_snapshot)
        AC->>Agent: invoke(market_data)
        Agent-->>AC: raw AgentOutput
        AC-->>Engine: validated AgentDecision[]
        loop Each decision
            Engine->>TE: execute(action, ticker, qty, price)
            TE->>P: apply_long_buy / apply_short_open / ...
        end
        Engine->>V: calculate_portfolio_value(P, prices)
        V-->>Engine: PortfolioValuePoint
        Engine->>O: format_daily_row(date, snapshot)
        opt 3+ data points
            Engine->>M: compute(equity_curve)
            M-->>Engine: PerformanceMetrics
        end
    end
    Engine-->>CLI: final PerformanceMetrics
</pre>
</div>

<div class="intro-box">
  <h3>🚶 Step-by-Step Walkthrough</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>CLI parses arguments</strong> — tickers, date range, model, analysts are passed to <code>BacktestEngine</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Data prefetch</strong> — prices, financials, insider trades, and news are bulk-downloaded for the date range, including SPY for benchmarking.</li>
    <li><strong>Daily loop begins</strong> — the engine iterates over business days (<code>pd.date_range(freq='B')</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Agent invoked</strong> — <code>AgentController</code> sends current prices + portfolio snapshot to the selected AI model and normalizes its response.</li>
    <li><strong>Trades executed</strong> — each <code>AgentDecision</code> is routed through <code>TradeExecutor</code>, which calls the appropriate <code>Portfolio</code> method.</li>
    <li><strong>Valuation &amp; exposures</strong> — positions are marked to market; long, short, gross, and net exposure are computed.</li>
    <li><strong>Metrics updated</strong> — after 3 data points, Sharpe, Sortino, and max drawdown are recalculated from the equity curve.</li>
    <li><strong>Results returned</strong> — the final <code>PerformanceMetrics</code> TypedDict is returned alongside the SPY benchmark comparison.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- ───────────── Interactions ───────────── -->
<h2 id="interactions">Interactions</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>AgentController</td><td>Method call</td><td>Passes date, prices, portfolio snapshot; receives validated decisions</td></tr>
  <tr><td>AgentController</td><td>Trading Agent</td><td>LLM API</td><td>Invokes the selected model with market context and retrieves trading signals</td></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>TradeExecutor</td><td>Method call</td><td>Routes each <code>AgentDecision</code> to the correct trade method</td></tr>
  <tr><td>TradeExecutor</td><td>Portfolio</td><td>Mutation</td><td>Calls <code>apply_long_buy</code>, <code>apply_short_open</code>, etc. to update positions &amp; cash</td></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>Valuation</td><td>Function call</td><td>Marks portfolio to market; computes exposure breakdown</td></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>Metrics</td><td>Method call</td><td>Feeds equity curve points; receives Sharpe, Sortino, drawdown</td></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>BenchmarkCalculator</td><td>Method call</td><td>SPY price series → buy-and-hold return for comparison</td></tr>
  <tr><td>BacktestEngine</td><td>OutputBuilder</td><td>Method call</td><td>Daily snapshot → formatted terminal table rows</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ───────────── Deep-Dive Hub ───────────── -->
<h2 id="deep-dives">Deep-Dive Topics</h2>
<div class="hub-note">
  The following cards cover the three core subsystems of the backtesting engine.
  Each represents a logical grouping of closely-related functionality.
</div>
<div class="card-grid">
  <div class="card">
    <h4>🔄 Backtest Loop <span class="focus-badge">Core</span></h4>
    <p>The event-driven loop that drives the entire simulation forward through business days.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Date iteration with <code>pd.date_range(freq='B')</code></li>
      <li>Data prefetch &amp; caching strategy</li>
      <li>Agent invocation → trade execution pipeline</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h4>💼 Portfolio Management <span class="focus-badge">Core</span></h4>
    <p>Cash, positions, margin tracking, and cost-basis accounting for long and short trades.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Long buy/sell and short open/cover flows</li>
      <li>Margin requirement enforcement</li>
      <li>Realized gains tracking per ticker</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h4>📊 Performance Metrics <span class="focus-badge">Core</span></h4>
    <p>Risk-adjusted return metrics computed from the portfolio equity curve.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sharpe ratio (annualized, risk-free adjusted)</li>
      <li>Sortino ratio (downside deviation only)</li>
      <li>Max drawdown with peak/trough dates</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

